GNU C Library (glibc)
---------------------
The Linux release binaries (linux_amd64, linux_arm64, and the .deb/.rpm
packages built from them) and the server in the Docker image
(ghcr.io/kodestar/audiosilo-server) are statically linked against the GNU C
Library, which is licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License,
version 2.1 or later (https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/lgpl-2.1.html).
macOS and Windows binaries do not contain glibc.

- The release binaries are built on GitHub's ubuntu-latest runner with
  Ubuntu's glibc packages (libc6-dev, and libc6-dev-arm64-cross for arm64).
  Source: https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/glibc and
  https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/cross-toolchain-base
- The Docker image's server is built in the golang:1.26 (Debian) image with
  Debian's glibc packages. Source: https://sources.debian.org/src/glibc/
- Upstream source: https://sourceware.org/glibc/

To relink AudioSilo against a modified glibc: the complete source of AudioSilo
and its build recipe are public at https://github.com/KodeStar/audiosilo-server
(the Linux build settings are the audiosilo-linux build in .goreleaser.yml and
the build stage of the Dockerfile). Build it with your glibc in place of the
distribution's.

On request we will provide the glibc source used for any published release:
kode@audiosilo.app.

